course: dictionary
lesson: 1085
title: Same sound, different word
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words sound alike but mean different things, so you must use the context to find the right meaning. «In PE, she wore a sports bra for extra support.» The words sports and support tell you this bra is clothing worn for exercise.
explain: A bra is a piece of underwear that women and older girls wear to support and cover their breasts. Bra is short for «brassiere». Many girls wear one as their body changes, and choosing what to wear is a personal decision.
explain: Now a clue from French. «Le bras ("BRA") is the arm.» Bras sounds like bra, but it is a different word from another language. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then check that your meaning still makes sense.
fact: A bra is a piece of underwear worn by women and older girls to support and cover their breasts.
fact: Bra is short for «brassiere».
fact: A «training bra» or «first bra» is a common choice for older girls.
fact: A «sports bra» gives extra support during exercise.
fact: «Le bras» means arm in French, and «une main» means hand. Words that sound alike can mean different things in different languages.
exercise: «In PE, she wore a sports bra for extra support.» What is a sports bra for? | Making her taller | Keeping her hands warm | *Extra support during exercise | Carrying her water bottle
exercise: In French, «le bras» is the arm. Which English word does bras sound like? | *Bra | Bridge | Brick | Bread
exercise: «Le bras» in French means which part of the body? | The hand | *The arm | The foot | The leg
test: Bra is short for which longer word? | *Brassiere | Bracelet | Bravery | Brasserie
test: Which sentence uses bra with its clothing meaning? | She painted her bra blue. | *She bought her first bra with her mum. | She rode her bra to school.
exam: Lily says bras in French means underwear, because it sounds like bra. Is she right? | Yes, bras means leg in French | *No, bras means arm in French, so it is a different word | No, bras means a hat in French | Yes, bras means underwear in every language
